/-!
# ptmalloc versions, glibc 2.40: the tcache-path code bytes and their instruction sequences

The per-version x86 data of the tcache paths for the pin `ubuntu_2_40_1ubuntu3_1` (glibc 2.40,
Ubuntu 2.40-1ubuntu3.1; `Silmaril.Libc.Ptmalloc.Versions.pin240`): the bytes of `__libc_malloc`
(820 at `0xb2c60`), `__libc_free` (271 at `0xb3370`) and `_int_free` (1019 at `0xb07c0`), transcribed
from the pinned file (`.text` file offsets equal virtual addresses; checked by
`scripts/ptmalloc/check-code.py`), and the fact that `__libc_malloc` carries gcc's inlined `tcache_get`
(`X86sim.TcGetSeq`) at offset 350 (2.39: 342; the sequence is the same eleven instructions,
only `jne`'s displacement differs), and that `_int_free` carries gcc's inlined `tcache_put`
(`X86sim.TcPutSeq`) at offset 472, exactly as in 2.39 but for the `tcache_key` displacement. With it, x86sim's generic run `X86sim.tcGetRun` (and every
block simulation built on it) holds for 2.40 with no new proof: `tcGetRun240`.

Same shape as `Silmaril.Proofs.Libc.Ptmalloc.X86sim.V239.Code` (x86sim's 2.39 module).
-/

